# pdf-craft

A command-line PDF toolkit built on Apache PDFBox 3. One fat JAR, zero configuration — generate, convert, manipulate, secure, sign, and inspect PDF files from the terminal or any scripting pipeline.

---

## Features at a glance

| Category | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Template generation** | Render PDFs from JSON data + template definitions. Tables, two-column layouts, headers, footers, metadata. |
| **Batch generation** | Process an entire directory of JSON files or a CSV in parallel. Optional PDF/A and signing on every output. |
| **HTML → PDF** | Convert any HTML file to PDF using wkhtmltopdf. Supports CSS, images, JavaScript, canvas, custom page sizes. |
| **Text extraction** | Pull plain text from any PDF, with page-range filtering and position-based sorting. |
| **Image extraction** | Export all embedded images from a PDF as PNG or JPEG. |
| **Merge** | Combine multiple PDFs into one, with optional metadata carry-over. |
| **Split** | Divide a PDF by page range, every-N-pages, or into N equal parts. |
| **Encryption** | AES-256 owner/user passwords with eight granular permission flags or named presets. |
| **Decryption** | Remove encryption with the owner password. Change passwords without re-generating. |
| **Digital signatures** | PKCS#7/CMS detached signatures from a PKCS12 keystore. RFC 3161 TSA timestamps. Visible signature boxes. |
| **Signature verification** | Verify all signatures in a PDF, export signer certificates. |
| **PDF/A compliance** | Attach ISO 19005-1 (PDF/A-1b) markers to any generated output. Preflight validation with detailed error reports. |
| **AcroForm generation** | Create interactive PDFs with text fields, checkboxes, radio buttons, combo boxes, and list boxes. |
| **AcroForm fill** | Fill existing form fields by name, with optional flatten-to-static for archival. |
| **AcroForm extraction** | Read field names, types, and current values as structured output. |
| **Rasterization** | Convert PDF pages to PNG or JPEG at any DPI. |
| **Printing** | Send a PDF to any installed printer with page range, copies, and duplex control. |
| **Security inspection** | Inspect encryption algorithm, key length, and permission flags on any PDF. |

---

## Requirements

- Java 17 or later
- Maven 3.8+ (to build from source)
- wkhtmltopdf 0.12.x — only required for `--html-to-pdf` mode

---

## Build

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-org/pdf-craft.git
cd pdf-craft
mvn package -q
# → target/pdf-creator-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar  (fat JAR, ~15 MB)
```

The Maven Shade plugin bundles all dependencies into a single executable JAR. No separate classpath setup needed.

---

## Quick start

```bash
alias pdf="java -jar target/pdf-creator-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar"

# Convert HTML to PDF
pdf --html-to-pdf --input report.html --output report.pdf

# Merge two PDFs
pdf --merge --inputs part1.pdf,part2.pdf --output combined.pdf

# Encrypt with AES-256, read-only for users
pdf --encrypt --input doc.pdf --output doc-secure.pdf \
    --owner-password admin123 --user-password view456 --preset read-only

# Sign with a PKCS12 keystore
pdf --sign --input doc.pdf --output doc-signed.pdf \
    --keystore my.p12 --keystore-password secret \
    --reason "Approved" --tsa-url http://timestamp.digicert.com
```

---

## Usage reference

### Template generation

Render a single PDF from a JSON data file and a template definition.

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --template-id  bank-statement \
  --data-file    data/CUST-001.json \
  --output       output/statement.pdf
```

**With custom template and config files:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --template-id   bank-statement \
  --template-file my-templates.json \
  --config-file   my-configs.json \
  --data-file     data/CUST-001.json \
  --output        output/statement.pdf
```

**With PDF/A-1b compliance:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --template-id bank-statement \
  --data-file   data/CUST-001.json \
  --output      output/statement.pdf \
  --pdfa
```

---

### Batch generation — JSON directory

One PDF per `.json` file in the data directory, using 8 parallel threads:

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --batch \
  --template-id  bank-statement \
  --data-dir     data/statements/ \
  --output-dir   output/statements/ \
  --threads      8
```

**Batch + PDF/A + sign in one pass:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --batch \
  --template-id       bank-statement \
  --data-dir          data/statements/ \
  --output-dir        output/signed/ \
  --threads           4 \
  --pdfa \
  --keystore          certs/bank.p12 \
  --keystore-password secret \
  --reason            "Monthly Account Statement" \
  --tsa-url           http://timestamp.digicert.com
```

---

### Batch generation — CSV

One PDF per data row. The CSV must have a header row.

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --batch \
  --template-id  notification-letter \
  --csv-file     data/customers.csv \
  --output-dir   output/letters/ \
  --threads      4
```

**CSV column configuration:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar \
  --batch \
  --template-id  notification-letter \
  --csv-file     data/customers.csv \
  --output-dir   output/letters/ \
  --ref-col      customer_id \
  --out-col      output_filename
```

---

### HTML → PDF

Requires wkhtmltopdf installed ([wkhtmltopdf.org](https://wkhtmltopdf.org/downloads.html)).

**Basic conversion:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --html-to-pdf \
  --input  invoice.html \
  --output invoice.pdf
```

**Full options — Letter landscape with print CSS and metadata:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --html-to-pdf \
  --input             report.html \
  --output            report.pdf \
  --page-size         Letter \
  --orientation       Landscape \
  --margin-top        15 \
  --margin-bottom     15 \
  --margin-left       20 \
  --margin-right      20 \
  --print-media-type \
  --title             "Q4 2025 Report" \
  --author            "Finance Team" \
  --subject           "Quarterly Business Review"
```

**JavaScript-rendered content (e.g. chart.js graphs):**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --html-to-pdf \
  --input            dashboard.html \
  --output           dashboard.pdf \
  --javascript \
  --javascript-delay 2000
```

**Configure wkhtmltopdf path on Windows (instead of environment variable):**

Create `pdf-creator.properties` next to the JAR:

```properties
wkhtmltopdf.path = C:/Program Files/wkhtmltopdf/bin/wkhtmltopdf.exe
```

Or pass it explicitly:

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --html-to-pdf \
  --input       invoice.html \
  --output      invoice.pdf \
  --tool-config C:/myapp/pdf-creator.properties
```

---

### Text extraction

```bash
# Extract all text to stdout
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --extract --input document.pdf

# Extract pages 2–5, write to file
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --extract \
  --input      document.pdf \
  --output     extracted.txt \
  --start-page 2 \
  --end-page   5

# Password-protected PDF
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --extract \
  --input    encrypted.pdf \
  --password userpassword
```

---

### Image extraction

```bash
# Extract all images as PNG
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --extract-images \
  --input      document.pdf \
  --output-dir extracted-images/

# Extract as JPEG, skip tiny images, page range
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --extract-images \
  --input      document.pdf \
  --output-dir images/ \
  --img-format jpg \
  --min-width  100 \
  --min-height 100 \
  --start-page 1 \
  --end-page   10
```

---

### Merge

```bash
# Merge two PDFs
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --merge \
  --inputs  part1.pdf,part2.pdf \
  --output  combined.pdf

# Merge three PDFs, one password-protected
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --merge \
  --inputs    public.pdf,secure.pdf,appendix.pdf \
  --passwords ,ownerpass, \
  --output    full-report.pdf
```

---

### Split

```bash
# Split by explicit page ranges
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --split \
  --input       report.pdf \
  --page-ranges "1-3,4-8,9-12" \
  --output-dir  split/

# Split every 5 pages
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --split \
  --input          large.pdf \
  --every-n-pages  5 \
  --output-dir     chunks/

# Divide into 4 equal parts
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --split \
  --input       book.pdf \
  --into-parts  4 \
  --output-dir  parts/
```

---

### Encryption (AES-256)

```bash
# Using a permission preset
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --encrypt \
  --input          document.pdf \
  --output         document-secure.pdf \
  --owner-password admin123 \
  --user-password  view456 \
  --preset         read-only

# Available presets: all-allowed | read-only | print-only | no-copy

# Using granular permission flags
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --encrypt \
  --input          document.pdf \
  --output         document-secure.pdf \
  --owner-password admin123 \
  --deny-copy \
  --deny-modify \
  --deny-annotations
```

---

### Decryption and password management

```bash
# Decrypt (remove all security)
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --decrypt \
  --input          secure.pdf \
  --output         plain.pdf \
  --owner-password admin123

# Change password
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --change-password \
  --input              secure.pdf \
  --output             re-encrypted.pdf \
  --owner-password     oldpassword \
  --new-owner-password newpassword \
  --new-user-password  newuserpass

# Inspect security settings (no password needed for permission-only encrypted PDFs)
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --inspect-security --input document.pdf

# Inspect when user password is set
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --inspect-security \
  --input          document.pdf \
  --owner-password admin123
```

---

### Digital signatures

**Sign with visible signature box and TSA timestamp:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --sign \
  --input            document.pdf \
  --output           document-signed.pdf \
  --keystore         my-cert.p12 \
  --keystore-password secret \
  --reason           "Approved by Finance" \
  --location         "London, UK" \
  --tsa-url          http://timestamp.digicert.com \
  --visible \
  --sig-page         1 \
  --sig-x            50 \
  --sig-y            50 \
  --sig-width        200 \
  --sig-height       60
```

**Verify all signatures in a PDF:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --verify --input document-signed.pdf
```

**Export signer certificate:**

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --export-cert \
  --input  document-signed.pdf \
  --output signer.crt
```

---

### PDF/A validation

```bash
# Validate against PDF/A-1b
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --validate-pdfa --input document.pdf

# Validate and write detailed JSON report
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --validate-pdfa \
  --input       document.pdf \
  --output      validation-report.json \
  --standard    PDF_A_1B
```

Exit codes: `0` = valid, `1` = invalid (see report for issues), `2` = error.

