### AcroForm — generate interactive PDF

*Note: This does not work properly*

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --generate-form \
  --form-def  forms/application-form.json \
  --output    output/application-form.pdf
```

---

### AcroForm — fill and flatten

*Note: This does not work properly*

```bash
# Fill fields interactively
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --fill-form \
  --input     forms/application-form.pdf \
  --fill-data data/applicant.json \
  --output    output/filled-form.pdf

# Fill and flatten (fields become static — for archival)
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --fill-form \
  --input     forms/application-form.pdf \
  --fill-data data/applicant.json \
  --output    output/archived-form.pdf \
  --flatten
```

---

### AcroForm — extract field values

*Note: This does not work properly*

```bash
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --extract-form \
  --input  forms/filled-form.pdf \
  --output extracted-fields.json
```

---

### Rasterization

Convert PDF pages to images:

```bash
# All pages as PNG at 150 DPI
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --rasterize \
  --input      document.pdf \
  --output-dir page-images/

# Pages 1–3 as JPEG at 300 DPI
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --rasterize \
  --input      document.pdf \
  --output-dir images/ \
  --format     jpg \
  --dpi        300 \
  --start-page 1 \
  --end-page   3
```

---

### Printing

```bash
# Print to default printer
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --print --input document.pdf

# Print specific pages to a named printer
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --print \
  --input      document.pdf \
  --printer    "Office HP LaserJet" \
  --start-page 1 \
  --end-page   5 \
  --copies     2

# List available printers
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --list-printers
```

---

## Chaining operations

The output of any mode is a standard PDF, so operations chain naturally:

```bash
# HTML → PDF → encrypt → sign
java -jar pdf-creator.jar --html-to-pdf \
    --input invoice.html --output invoice.pdf

java -jar pdf-creator.jar --encrypt \
    --input invoice.pdf --output invoice-enc.pdf \
    --owner-password admin --preset read-only

java -jar pdf-creator.jar --sign \
    --input invoice-enc.pdf --output invoice-final.pdf \
    --keystore my.p12 --keystore-password secret
```

---

## Template format

Templates are defined in `templates/pdf-templates.json`:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "bank-statement",
    "title": "Account Statement",
    "sections": [
      { "type": "summary", "fields": ["accountName", "accountNumber", "period"] },
      { "type": "table",   "dataKey": "transactions",
        "columns": ["date", "description", "debit", "credit", "balance"] }
    ],
    "footer": { "text": "{{bankName}} · {{sortCode}}", "pageNumbers": true }
  }
]
```

Data files use `{{placeholder}}` syntax for scalar values and arrays for table rows. See `data/statements/CUST-001.json` for a complete example.

---

## Configuration presets

Config presets in `configs/pdf-configs.json` define page size, fonts, margins, and colours:

```json
[
  {
    "id":        "default",
    "pageSize":  "A4",
    "font":      "Helvetica",
    "fontSize":  10,
    "margins":   { "top": 40, "bottom": 40, "left": 50, "right": 50 },
    "headerBg":  "#1B3A6B",
    "headerFg":  "#FFFFFF"
  }
]
```

Pass a different config at runtime with `--config-id` or `--config-file`.

---

## Dependencies

| Library | Version | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Apache PDFBox | 3.0.2 | Core PDF read/write engine |
| PDFBox Preflight | 3.0.2 | PDF/A-1 validation |
| PDFBox XMPBox | 3.0.2 | XMP metadata for PDF/A |
| BouncyCastle Provider | 1.78.1 | AES-256 encryption |
| BouncyCastle PKIX | 1.78.1 | CMS signatures, certificate handling |
| BouncyCastle Util | 1.78.1 | TSA timestamp embedding |
| JAXB API | 2.3.1 | XML/XMP support on Java 17+ |
| wkhtmltopdf | 0.12.x | HTML rendering (external binary, `--html-to-pdf` only) |

All Java dependencies are bundled into the fat JAR by Maven Shade. No classpath configuration required.

---

## Project structure

```
pdf-craft/
├── src/main/java/com/pdfcreator/
│   ├── PdfCreator.java              Main entry point — CLI routing
│   ├── batch/                       Batch job orchestration
│   ├── extractor/                   Text and image extraction
│   ├── forms/                       AcroForm generation, filling, extraction
│   ├── generator/                   Core PDF page generation
│   ├── htmlconverter/               HTML-to-PDF via wkhtmltopdf
│   ├── manipulator/                 Merge and split
│   ├── pdfa/                        PDF/A compliance attachment
│   ├── pipeline/                    Template render pipeline
│   ├── printer/                     Java Printing API integration
│   ├── rasterizer/                  Page-to-image rendering
│   ├── renderer/                    Section renderers (table, summary, columns)
│   ├── security/                    Encryption, decryption, permissions
│   ├── signature/                   Digital signatures and verification
│   ├── template/                    Template loading and placeholder resolution
│   └── validator/                   PDF/A preflight validation
├── src/test/java/com/pdfcreator/
│   └── PdfCreatorTest.java          62 integration test scenarios
├── templates/
│   └── pdf-templates.json           Sample template definitions
├── configs/
│   └── pdf-configs.json             Sample config presets
├── data/
│   └── statements/                  Sample JSON data files
├── pdf-creator.properties           wkhtmltopdf path config (Windows / custom installs)
└── pom.xml
```

---

## Running the tests

```bash
mvn test
```

The test suite (`PdfCreatorTest.java`) covers 62 scenarios across all modes: template generation, batch processing, text/image extraction, merge/split, encryption, signing, PDF/A validation, AcroForm operations, rasterization, and HTML-to-PDF conversion.

